/**
 * @page neural_parameter_mapping_chapter Neural policies and parameter mapping
 *
 * @ref FeedForwardNetworkConfiguration defines the layer widths, activations,
 * and shared bias setting. @ref FeedForwardNetwork turns that value into an
 * owned sequence of @ref DenseLayer objects. @ref FeedForwardPolicy adapts the
 * resulting vector transformation to the typed @ref Policy interface.
 *
 * @image html neural_parameter_flow.svg "Feed-forward data flow and canonical parameter slices."
 *
 * @section neural_construction Network construction
 *
 * Let \f$n_0\f$ be `input_size`, let the configured hidden widths be
 * \f$n_1,\ldots,n_{L-1}\f$, and let \f$n_L\f$ be `output_size`. Hidden layers
 * are created in vector order and share `hidden_activation`; the final layer
 * uses `output_activation`. A network with no hidden widths contains one dense
 * layer from input directly to output.
 *
 * Layer \f$\ell\f$ stores
 * \f$W^{(\ell)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n_\ell\times n_{\ell-1}}\f$ and, when
 * `use_bias` is true, \f$b^{(\ell)}\in\mathbb{R}^{n_\ell}\f$. Propagation is
 *
 * \f[
 * h^{(0)}=x_t,\qquad
 * h^{(\ell)}=\phi_\ell\!\left(W^{(\ell)}h^{(\ell-1)}+b^{(\ell)}\right),
 * \quad \ell=1,\ldots,L.
 * \f]
 *
 * @ref ActivationFunction applies the selected @ref ActivationType element by
 * element. @ref DenseLayer checks its input dimension before the matrix product.
 * @ref FeedForwardPolicy additionally rejects a non-finite final output before
 * constructing an action.
 *
 * @section neural_layout Canonical parameter layout
 *
 * @ref FeedForwardNetworkConfiguration::parameterCountFromConfiguration uses
 * checked arithmetic for
 *
 * \f[
 * d=\sum_{\ell=1}^{L}\left(n_\ell n_{\ell-1}+\beta n_\ell\right),
 * \qquad \beta=\mathbf{1}_{use\_bias}\in\{0,1\}.
 * \f]
 *
 * One canonical vector concatenates layers in propagation order. Each layer
 * contributes all entries of \f$W^{(\ell)}\f$ in Eigen column-major order
 * followed by \f$b^{(\ell)}\f$ when enabled. For a matrix position
 * \f$(i,j)\f$, the layer-local weight offset is \f$j n_\ell+i\f$.
 * @ref ParameterLayout stores the network-wide
 * `weights_offset`, `weights_count`, `biases_offset`, and `biases_count` for
 * each layer.
 *
 * `FeedForwardNetwork::setParameters()` partitions the candidate vector by
 * complete layer slices and @ref DenseLayer maps each weight slice directly to
 * its matrix dimensions. `parameters()` reconstructs the same interleaved
 * layer layout. `weightsParameters()` concatenates only layer weights;
 * `biasesParameters()` concatenates only layer biases. Policy regularization
 * consumes the weight-only vector, so biases never enter its L1 or squared-L2
 * penalty.
 *
 * @section neural_policy_adapter Policy inference
 *
 * 1. `Observation::observationToVector()` returns components in configured
 *    input order.
 * 2. @ref FeedForwardNetwork::forward propagates the vector through every layer.
 * 3. A default-constructed action receives the output through
 *    `Action::vectorToAction()`.
 * 4. The populated action is returned by value to @ref EpisodeRunner.
 *
 * Template checks require observation and action types derived from
 * @ref ObservationBase and @ref ActionBase, and require a default-constructible
 * action. @ref PolicyFactory validates configuration values and returns unique
 * ownership of either a typed policy or a raw network.
 *
 * @section neural_serialization Serialization
 *
 * @ref PolicySerialization writes version 1 as ordered comma-separated rows:
 * format version, policy type, input width, hidden widths, output width,
 * activations, bias flag, regularization settings, and canonical parameters.
 * Double values use `max_digits10`. Deserialization requires the same row order,
 * rejects unsupported or trailing data, validates finite numeric values, and
 * reconstructs the policy to verify the parameter count. The returned
 * configuration and parameter vector own all parsed data.
 *
 * @section neural_cost Neural computation metric
 *
 * @ref FeedForwardNetworkComputationCost counts
 * \f$\sum_{\ell=1}^{L}n_{\ell-1}n_\ell\f$ multiply-accumulate operations per inference. Bias
 * additions and activation operations fall outside this MAC metric.
 * @ref PolicyOptimizationProblem multiplies it by the episode step count because
 * it performs one policy inference before every simulator step.
 *
 * @see @ref simulation_execution_chapter "Simulation and policy execution"
 * @see @ref optimization_lifecycle_chapter "Optimization lifecycle"
 * @see @ref technical_chapters "Technical Chapters"
 */
